10
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Hilary and Jackie is a 1998 British biographical film directed by Anand Tucker, starring Emily Watson and Rachel
Griffiths as the British classical musician sisters Jacqueline du Pré (cello) and Hilary du Pré (flute).

11
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:39,000
The film covers Jacqueline's meteoric rise to fame, her alleged affair with Hilary's husband Christopher "Kiffer" Finzi, and
her struggle with multiple sclerosis starting in her late 20s ultimately leading to her death at the age of 42.

12
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Frank Cottrell-Boyce wrote the screenplay at the same time that siblings Hilary and Piers du Pré were working on their
memoir, published in 1997 as A Genius in the Family (later republished under the title Hilary and Jackie).

13
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
As such, the film's closing credits states that it is based on the memoir, though Cottrell-Boyce confirmed, in a programme distributed
at early showings of the film, that: "Hilary was working on the book at the same time as I was working on the film ...

14
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:48,000
it was at a very early stage when we were doing the script".

15
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
The film was not intended as a documentary and thus, unlike the book, does not
claim to be the true story and includes some fictionalised incidents.

16
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
When it was released, the film attracted controversy when several personal friends of Jacqueline publicly condemned it for allegedly
distorting details in her life, while Hilary publicly defended it as her and Piers's version of the family's story.

17
01:42:51,000 --> 01:42:57,000
Hilary and Jackie generally received critical acclaim, and both Griffiths and Watson were nominated
for an Academy Award, for Best Supporting Actress and Best Actress, respectively.

18
01:48:54,000 --> 01:49:00,000
The film explores themes of career, london, england,
concert, sibling relationship, musician.

19
01:54:57,000 --> 01:55:03,000
The tone is emotional.
